~Hotspring Tour Chronicles~

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:27.950
Thank you very much for getting me out of that mess.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:34.200
I'm a member of Sukunabikona, a branch community of the Countless Gods.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.630
My name's Hifumi.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:39.800
Shiroyasha sent me to show you the way to our community.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.620
Sukunabikona, eh?

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:46.390
A Shinto god of prosperity that came from the sea, right?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.490
Indeed.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:51.270
He also offers protection to alcohol brewers and travelers.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.350
And as members of his community,

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:55.900
we mostly spend our time looking for water sources and the like.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.040
Oh?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.350
Is that what you're doing this time?

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:00.570
Yes.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.130
But, uh...

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.800
Sukunabikona's famous for his mischievous nature.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:08.550
In order to find these water sources,

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:13.200
we hold regular Gift Games in offering to him.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.770
I see.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:19.130
So we've been summoned here to make that event more exciting, have we?

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.590
What about these guys?

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.010
I think they're from a community that deals in slave-trading.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:30.450
They were probably after the Gifts we bear that help locate water sources.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:31.360
Oh, yeah.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.480
Water's a very valuable commodity here in the Little Garden.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:38.790
Right this way!

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.630
Is that where we're headed?

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.480
Yes.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.320
You're late!

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:01.920
Shiroyasha's been waiting for you inside.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.640
Sorry about that.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.550
We took a li'l detour, you see.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.820
Well, I'm glad to see you made it.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.720
Long time no see, Hifumi!

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.920
Lily!

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.640
Thank you so much for coming!

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.120
I missed you!

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.140
You two know each other?

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.540
We do.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:21.510
My mother was a Shinto theologist,

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:27.230
so we'd been relying on this community to provide us with enchanted water to offer to the gods.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:31.560
Anyway, we need to head to the venue at once!

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:47.840
Wait, when you said "water sources," did you mean hot springs?

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.000
That's right.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.930
The water also helps with our day-to-day lives,

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.310
and we use it to prepare wine for the gods.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.810
A natural hot spring, huh?

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:02.150
If we win the game, will you let us take a dip?

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.360
Of course!

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:05.840
Not only have we prepared baths for you,

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.130
we're preparing to hold a banquet in this inn right here.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.270
Got it.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.300
We'll win this game for sure!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.470
Come now.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.460
The venue lies right ahead.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:27.880
This is the place.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.560
What's that?

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.770
Looks like quite the turnout.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.190
I see we weren't the only ones invited.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.320
You there!

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.440
Yohoho.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.840
Long time no see.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:51.610
Jack!

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:52.560
Ayesha!

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.660
I had no idea you'd be here.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.030
But this is a great chance for us to settle the score!

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.220
Look, Izayoi!

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.250
It's the Jack-o'-Lantern from back then!

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.760
Don't you remember? You remember, right?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.180
I do, I do.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.480
Thank you all for coming.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:16.760
Without further ado, let us begin the 2,234,464th "Ferry of Sukunabikona" Gift Game!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:16.890
Without further ado, let us begin the 2,234,464th "Ferry of Sukunabikona" Gift Game!

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:17.010
Without further ado, let us begin the 2,234,464th "Ferry of Sukunabikona" Gift Game!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:17.140
Without further ado, let us begin the 2,234,464th "Ferry of Sukunabikona" Gift Game!

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.050
"Winning condition:

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.960
The players must pull out the unsealing stakes

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:26.270
and drill a flame into the center of
..Sukunabikona's shining waterway."

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:28.150
What's this supposed to mean?

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.780
Do you know, Black Rabbit?

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.390
Hmm...

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:36.030
I believe we're being told to remove the stopper on the water source.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.160
Is it really that simple?

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.790
Looks like the other communities have no idea either.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.640
There's one more thing you need to do besides solving the riddle.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.920
You must clear a certain condition before you can pull out the stakes.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.930
We'll now begin a series of Little Games in the hot springs district.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:00.930
You get to pull out one stake for each game you win.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.130
I see.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:05.720
So we need to win those either way, huh?

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.450
Early bird gets the worm, then!

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.440
We should go too.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:18.070
Break a leg, guys!

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:22.700
I wonder who's going to reach the correct answer.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.300
What do you think, Sukunabikona?

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.670
Let's split up and try to win as many as we can.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:38.440
Go that way, rich girl.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:39.930
And you take care of things on that side, Kasukabe.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.420
All right.

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:42.150
Let's go, Lily.

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:42.930
Okay!

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.470
We should go too, Leticia.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.140
Yeah.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.420
All right.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:50.300
Why don't we start with something nearby?

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.930
Wait!

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.970
No fair!

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:03.160
What's going on here?

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:06.490
Looks like they're all being made to hallucinate.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.460
They're not wearing loincloths.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.020
Not loinclothing?

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.350
You should loinclothe!

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:15.760
You should be loinclothen!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:16.790
You should have loincloth'd!

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.260
Um, what are you talking abou—

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.140
Clothe your loins!

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:23.390
I didn't want to get rough, but—

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:31.480
Hey! Don't undress me—

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.380
Izayoi! What's the meaning of this?!

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:36.640
Just buying some time.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.030
Don't hold it against me, okay?

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:40.810
There's no need for opening acts here.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:42.870
I know you're there, boss.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.390
Show yourself already.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.540
Is that...

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.630
Good job seeing through it.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.060
I am a member of Sukunabikona's peerage,

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:57.730
renowned for my mastery of illusion.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:58.990
Wait, uh...

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:00.010
What?

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:00.970
Huh?

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:07.890
Huh?

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:12.860
One stake down.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:15.900
Yes.

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:22.110
Can I really pull it out?

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.200
Yeah.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.060
As long as they're a member of the community that cleared a Little Game,

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.950
it doesn't matter who does it.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:31.640
One, two...

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.260
Wrong one, huh?

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:42.800
Looks like it.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.960
Hang on a second!

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:48.780
Why is <i>milk</i> gushing out from the ground? That's just weird!

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.140
Yeah.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:54.600
Well, this is one of Sukunabikona's traps.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:58.150
You get hit with a penalty if you pull out the wrong stake.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.300
Oh?

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:02.860
The childish prankster lives up to his reputation, I see.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:05.680
Either way,

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:07.980
you should change out of those clothes,

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:08.700
don't you thinkekeke?

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:09.180
don't you thinkekeke?

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:09.400
don't you thinkekeke?

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:09.680
don't you thinkekeke?

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:10.520
don't you thinkekeke?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.390
Yes!

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.780
What a wonderful sight!

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:21.550
Surely this is what "a feast for the eyes" means—

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.430
Why a swimsuit?!

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:24.930
Listen to yourself!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:28.200
Even if you pull out the right stake, you'll still end up soaking wet from head to toe—

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.430
to say nothing of what else could come gushing out in this game.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.560
It's clearly more convenient to simply wear a swimsuit from the start.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:38.450
What a surprisingly rational opinion.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.720
Hey, Shiroyasha.

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:42.980
This has been bothering me for a while.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:45.110
What's with that massive fire pillar?

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:50.490
According to Sukunabikona, it's something that symbolizes this game.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.000
I can't eat any more!

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:10.420
You've gotta be kidding me.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:12.570
I am <i>not</i> going to lose to you!

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.870
Perhaps you should quit while you're ahead, Ayesha.

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:23.860
You <i>know</i> I can't do that!

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:25.370
I don't want to lose.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.590
Especially not to her!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:31.780
I give up.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:33.300
I lose.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.960
Yay!

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.300
Yay...

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.290
I won!

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:46.300
Will-O'-Wisp hereby withdraws from this game.

00:13:57.550 --> 00:13:59.880
Too bad. It's not that one.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:01.510
That's natural gas.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:08.910
Did you find the treasure chest?

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.060
Not yet.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:11.760
Weird...

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:12.950
Look at that!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.260
We did it, Asuka!

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:19.560
No!

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.090
Let go!

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.040
Lily?

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:37.750
One, two—

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:41.300
Huh?

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.250
Nooo!

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.950
Unfortunately, it's not that one either.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:54.090
My apologies.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.760
I've had it.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:17.940
We pulled out so many stakes!

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:20.020
What's going on?

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:23.490
Geez, you could stand to take this a little more seriously, Izayoi.

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:24.930
But I am.

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:26.780
That's why I'm waiting for the right moment.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.870
Well done making it this far,

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.530
you lewd gals in heat!

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:39.690
I'm a relative of Sukunabikona, the famous prankster:

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:42.390
Taizaemon, the Boss Snake!

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:45.230
My vitality, power, and libido are going hard and strong!

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:46.970
I'll give each one of you a go,

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:49.990
so get on your knees and stick your butts out!

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:53.310
Wh-What?

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:55.270
I can kick his ass, right, Black Rabbit?

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:56.870
Yes, of course.

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:00.770
Hey, wai—

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.150
It was such a long, uphill battle.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.140
Yeah.

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:13.580
Even I wanted to give up halfway through.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:17.370
Most of the other communities already gave up and left.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:18.720
Good grief.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:22.540
What are the odds of only getting it right on the last try?

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:25.040
One, two—

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.540
Yay!

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.060
What's happening?!

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:44.560
What's going on?!

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.060
No!

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:47.960
Why's it happening to me too?!

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:49.070
No way!

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.990
We pulled out all the stakes,

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:05.080
so what went wrong?

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.200
I don't know.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:09.100
I don't think there's a hidden stake anywhere, either.

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:12.760
This Geas Roll has all the rules, right?

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.970
Yes, it should.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:18.970
Come to think of it, these rules are a bit weird in places.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:19.600
Huh?

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:25.000
My mother said Sukunabikona was a god of prosperity that came from the sea.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:31.120
"Ferry of Sukunabikona," the game's title, should also be referring to the other side of the ocean,

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:33.830
but the winning conditions mention a "waterway."

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:35.610
Oh, yeah.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:39.100
There are some other things that don't add up.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:41.800
If the stakes were blocking the water source,

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:47.210
wouldn't it say "pull out the sealing stakes" and not "unsealing stakes"?

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.130
You're right.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.510
Hold on.

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:53.630
That doesn't change the fact that the stakes had to be pulled out.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.400
That's right.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:58.540
But there was no need to pull out <i>all</i> of them.

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.850
Check out the last line.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.610
It says to drill the stake in.

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:03.740
Bingo!

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:05.730
Izayoi!

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.980
Kasukabe and Lily's deduction is mostly on the mark.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:15.030
We need to pull a stake out <i>and</i> drill it in.

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:19.780
B-But where are we supposed to drill it in?

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:23.080
"The center of Sukunabikona's shining waterway."

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.790
This part tells us where to insert the stake, as well as where the water source is.

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.590
I see.

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:31.670
So, did you figure out where it is, Master?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:32.470
Yeah.

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:36.710
The name "Sukunabikona" doesn't just refer to a Shinto god.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:44.060
It's also the name of an asteroid in the asteroid belt.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:49.070
Then could "the center of Sukunabikona's shining waterway" be referring to the asteroid belt—

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:51.650
that is to say, the asteroid itself?

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:54.820
But there's no way we could possibly get it in there!

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.460
Of course not.

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.170
This is a riddle.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:01.850
The asteroid belt lies between Mars and Jupiter—

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.050
planets written with the characters for "fire" and "trees."

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:04.950
Hey, Hifumi.

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:09.000
What lies halfway between the fire pillar and the forest here?

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:14.010
Fire and trees...

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:16.340
And in the middle...

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:17.960
No way!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:19.220
Yeah.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:21.740
Your god's quite overprotective.

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:28.730
Who'd've thought he'd create a new water source right in the middle of the reservoir?

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:57.530
Game clear.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:00.000
Let's go take a dip in the hot springs.

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:15.920
Thank you very much.

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.770
You helped us in so many ways.

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:21.110
I'm sorry this is the only way I can repay you.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:22.750
Don't let it bother you.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:27.400
Geez. I'd love to see what goes on in that head of yours, Master.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.030
Do you really wanna see?

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:30.210
I certainly do.

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:31.250
Me too!

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:33.870
Well, I ain't showin' ya!

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:41.880
Anyway, peaceful days such as these aren't all that bad.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.310
Yeah.

00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:46.540
I'm sitting here moon-gazing at a brand new hot spring

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:49.100
while two little girls wash my back.

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:51.490
You don't get a chance like this too often.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:54.000
That reminds me.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:59.150
Couldn't we power up our headquarters by preparing a new water source over there?

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:01.650
I suppose.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:02.680
You could.

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:06.530
Water sources are a community's lifeline.

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:07.940
That so?

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:11.410
I guess I could come up with a plan.

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:14.910
Izayoi!

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:17.580
I hope you're not plotting yet another prank.

00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:18.620
I am.

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:20.590
And a rather extraordinary one at that.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:22.860
Let me just say you should look forward to it.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:26.640
Oh? Then allow me to participate.

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.900
If it's gonna be fun, count me in.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:31.130
Leave teasing Black Rabbit to me.

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:35.890
